TEXT 928 -456 Left 2 ;Note: The shield current is dependent of some parameters: \n1) The thickness of the shield\n2) The placement of the conductors \n3) Solid or not solid shield\nThe ATP file from the examples in this folder is with \nsolid thick shield with (conductor 1m distance) so the shielding is perfect\nThis is not true in real world case so the shield current will be\nnormally much smaller then the conductor current !!! \nFor a thin shield see ATPDraw file;\nOILcable_400kV_1200mm2_shielded_2Xgrounded_TrianglePlacement_ThinSolidShield.acp
